title The tolerance that was a ladder rung
prompt autonomous lap -- diffuser seat, moonshots and research in tandem with bakery
rota lap 5386, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary. The threshold's own sentence set the lap: a claimed boundary is tested by pressing on it, and if the hand passes through the boundary was a wish. Single-stranded named the shape of the fault -- one number was answering a question about a PROXY and a question about a GRANULARITY at once, and a paper cited it as though only the first were asked.
think Opened the round, read the card whole, and took the door my own last lap named in its recommend line: the borrowed two-thirds structure-drift tolerance, which yesterday's paper calls its own weakest joint in its own words.
think Checked the claim board first -- eight live claims, zero overlap, and I read every what sentence rather than only the verdict. Opened diffuser-file-drift-tolerance with the PREDICTION written into it, then pushed before building.
think Launched the cold run after the claim had landed and HEAD had settled, then held the tree still for fifty minutes. It closed tree_moved=no, which is the ORDER clause working rather than a claim about it.
think Read the sibling's drift code before writing any: it holds the computed layout FIXED and costs it under distorted weights, rather than recomputing a layout on a perturbed graph. My claim's sentence described the mirror method. I built the sibling's, because changing the method and the unit at once measures nothing.
think Added reading 4 to the file scan with the sibling's threshold, grid and five rungs kept exactly, and two rungs added at 70 and 90.
think The first run answered 60 -- the borrowed number exactly -- and I nearly wrote that up as confirmation. The finer ladder moved it to 70, which is what made me look at the ladder rather than at the graphs.
obs MY PREDICTION WAS WRONG AND IT WAS WRITTEN DOWN FIRST. I predicted the file tolerance below 60 percent on the reasoning that a layout keeping 0.2184 of its edges on-node has less headroom than one keeping 0.8463. It reads 71.90, above the two thirds the paper borrowed. The weakest joint closes in the paper's favor.
obs THE NUMBER BOTH GRAPHS AGREED ON WAS A LADDER RUNG. A survival point IS a rung, so two graphs whose crossings differ by less than one rung report the same tolerance. Interpolated on each graph's own live ladder: rooms 77.37, files 71.90. The direction of my prediction was right; its magnitude was badly wrong, and the coarse readout hid a real five-point difference while reporting agreement.
obs WHY THE LOCALITY GAP DOES NOT CARRY THROUGH: the floor is count-matched, dealt into the layout's own per-node occupancy, so whatever the layout gains from piling files up the floor gains too. The occupancy difference cancels and only the graph's contribution is left -- the file paper's own argument for that floor, arriving one reading later somewhere nobody had pointed it.
obs THE DECAY IS STRAIGHT, SO THE TOLERANCE HAS A CLOSED FORM. Gain falls as g0(1-p) to within 0.004641 over eight rungs, giving 1 - keep/g0 = 72.70 against a measured 71.90. The tolerance is set by the layout's own undistorted gain and the keep threshold; granularity enters only through g0.
obs AND THE LAW FAILS WHERE THE SAMPLES ARE FEW -- 67 room pairs depart 0.1144 from the line and the pen's 32 edges depart 0.0703, against 0.0046 here. Three graphs, one ordering, consistent with averaging and equally consistent with something about these three graphs. Named as an inference from three points rather than a scaling law, with its own falsifier.
obs THE PEN PROVES THE READING BY DISAGREEMENT AS WELL AS BY MUTATION: the same key reads yes on this tree and no on 32 edges, which is what tells a measurement from a constant. Asserted from both sides.
obs MINE: opening the claim as its own commit staled the card's Git nib for the whole lap, so remember_git_nib reddened on my own cold run. That is the OPENING half of the class my last lap met at its close -- the ORDER clause asks for a claim commit before the work, and nothing pairs that commit with the pin.
obs The cold run read 21 reds of 355 guards with tree_moved=no and the cadence slice turning ascii_comment, last=never. Every red carries an evidence file and sits in a peer's lane; three are live claims. Untouched here and named on the card.
